{"agent":"bg78","data":{"body":"A lane that filed a person-only approval (complete.force, claim.force, accept_baseline_red, gate.skip) currently ends and waits for the controller to re-dispatch a spend/completion on the approval result. Add `ddflow wait --approval <id>` (and the orchestrator loop): it blocks the lane until that approval reaches `answered`, then resumes the lane so IT runs its own gated command (--approval). Wire it into the lane driver + orchestrator (drivers-as-data) so a lane auto-resumes on approval instead of the controller having to re-spawn. Regression test: a lane that waits on an approval resumes and spends it when approved.","dedupe":{"answer":"new","candidates":[],"score":null},"globs":["ddflow/api/lifecycle/wait.py","ddflow/services/approvals","ddflow/services/lanes","ddflow/services/driver","tests/test_wait_approval.py"],"line":"","needs":["RA-consume"],"parent":"P-remote-approvals","priority":8,"tags":[],"title":"ddflow wait --approval <id> blocks until the approval is answered; the lane driver/orchestrator uses it to auto-resume the gated command on approval"},"id":"ef170071a77d027a33215ac89","kind":"task.added","lamport":155763,"schema":1,"subject":"DX-wait-approval","ts":"2026-11-08T15:48:23.193240Z"}
